Changes relative to the ScalableLux base
(full rationale and measurements: docs/NEW-ENGINE-TEARDOWN.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
  A. The update path was replaced by an own implementation (the reason this release exists; all
     three switches ship ON and can each be turned off with a system property):
     1. The edit is propagated and installed inside the setBlockState call that made it, instead of
        being handed to the light engine's queue (`-Dscalablelux.ownEdit=false` restores the base
        path).
     2. Edits are buffered per chunk, so one engine call handles a whole burst.
     3. The block-light decrease queue is seeded per chunk and drained once per burst instead of
        once per touched chunk (`-Dscalablelux.batchDecrease=false` restores the base path).
     4. A bulk skylight change is settled by a windowed recompute - only the y range an edit can
        reach (change +- 16, exact for levels 0..15) is recomputed, from the same propagation rule
        the base uses (`-Dscalablelux.recomputeSky=false` restores the base path).
     5. Inline guards are hoisted from per-change to per-chunk, and a change that makes an already
        dark cell fully opaque skips block-light seeding (provably cannot move block light).
     The light these produce is bit-identical to the base and to vanilla on the verification box
     used for acceptance (fingerprint sky=905931078dfc5ace block=59e2252f732ce67b).
  B. Identity: modId `lucistarlink`, display name `LuciStarlink`, entrypoint/command/mixin-config renamed.
     Internal ScalableLux identifiers (the `scalablelux$` mixin member prefix, the
     `ca.spottedleaf.starlight` packages) are deliberately kept so the origin of every file stays visible.
  C. Telemetry: periodic `SLTELEM` line (queue depth, dirty positions, pooled propagators),
     `-Dscalablelux.telemetrySeconds` (default 30, 0 disables).
  D. Commands: `/lucistarlink stats | light <pos> | relight <radius>` (permission level 2).
  E. Client update path: `SWMRNibbleArray.updateVisible()` no longer publishes a nibble whose bytes are
     unchanged (identity-preserving: only when the on-wire content is byte-identical). The client is
     not taken over: it runs the base path, and change A is consumed only under a
     "is a ServerLevel and is the server thread" guard.
  F. Save guarantees: the light-incorrect marks written to a save are per chunk and precise instead of
     blanket, and the worldgen write path was audited and pinned.
  G. Block-state opacity is cached per block state (0..15, or "not cached") so the propagation loop
     does not rebuild a palette lookup per neighbour.
  H. Compatibility: Sable per-plot light engines are deferred to Sable; Starlight / ScalableLux / Lucis
     are declared incompatible in the mod metadata.
  I. Instrumentation: `ca.spottedleaf.starlight.common.debug.LuxProfiler`, off unless
     `-Dscalablelux.profile=true`; `-Dscalablelux.recomputeDebug=true` prints per-settle phase timings.
  J. An optional, default-off scheduling batch (`-Dscalablelux.batchLimit`) kept for A/B experiments
     only; measured neutral, not enabled.
  K. Six further approaches were implemented, measured and closed; their code has been removed rather
     than left behind a flag: whole-chunk sky recompute, a flat byte-per-cell light mirror (two forms),
     a per-cell material table, a small-burst dispatch rule, flush batching, and deferring the
     block-light half. The numbers are in docs/NEW-ENGINE-TEARDOWN.md.
